### DNS Resolution Security and Efficiency

DNS resolution should be handled using secure libraries that support fallback mechanisms, such as `getaddrinfo` with multiple addresses. Use a thread-safe DNS resolver library like `c-ares`.

```c
#include <ares.h>

int resolve_dns(const char* hostname) {
    ares_channel channel;
    ares_init(&channel);
    struct addrinfo hints = {0};
    hints.ai_family = AF_UNSPEC;
    int status = ares_getaddrinfo(channel, hostname, NULL, &hints, &res);
    if (status != ARES_SUCCESS) {
        ares_destroy(channel);
        return -1; // DNS resolution failed
    }
    ares_freeaddrinfo(res);
    ares_destroy(channel);
    return 0;
}
